{"name":"Walled Garden","hex":"#11cc44","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"walled garden","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A garden enclosed by walls for purposes of shelter or decoration.","Any closed platform. A closed platform is any computing system where the manufacturer retains monopolistic control over installation, distribution, and use of software and services."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/walled_garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Walled garden","blocks":[{"text":"A walled garden is a garden enclosed by high walls, especially when this is done for horticultural rather than security purposes, although originally all gardens may have been enclosed for protection from animal or human intruders. In temperate climates, especially colder areas, such as Scotland, the essential function of the walling of a garden is to shelter the garden from wind and frost, though it may also serve a decorative purpose. Kitchen gardens were very often walled, which segregated them socially, allowing the gardeners, who were usually expected to vanish from the \"pleasure gardens\" when the occupants of the house were likely to be about, to continue their work. The walls, which were sometimes heated, also carried fruit trees trained as espaliers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Edzell_garden.JPG/330px-Edzell_garden.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walled_garden","wikidata":"Q7963015"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden","wikidata":"Q1107656"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/The_Lover_and_Dame_Oyseuse_outside_a_walled_garden_-_Roman_de_la_Rose_%28c.1490-1500%29%2C_f.12v_-_BL_Harley_MS_4425_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-The_Lover_and_Dame_Oyseuse_outside_a_walled_garden_-_Roman_de_la_Rose_%28c.1490-1500%29%2C_f.12v_-_BL_Harley_MS_4425_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/The_Lover_and_Dame_Oyseuse_outside_a_walled_garden_-_Roman_de_la_Rose_%28c.1490-1500%29%2C_f.12v_-_BL_Harley_MS_4425_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-The_Lover_and_Dame_Oyseuse_outside_a_walled_garden_-_Roman_de_la_Rose_%28c.1490-1500%29%2C_f.12v_-_BL_Harley_MS_4425_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Detail of miniature, c. 1490s, showing a garden walled all round, with internal fencing of various kinds.  The stone walls are unrealistically low for artistic convenience.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Lover_and_Dame_Oyseuse_outside_a_walled_garden_-_Roman_de_la_Rose_(c.1490-1500)%2C_f.12v_-_BL_Harley_MS_4425_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Meister_des_Frankfurter_Paradiesg%C3%A4rtleins_001.jpg/500px-Meister_des_Frankfurter_Paradiesg%C3%A4rtleins_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Meister_des_Frankfurter_Paradiesg%C3%A4rtleins_001.jpg/1280px-Meister_des_Frankfurter_Paradiesg%C3%A4rtleins_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Meister_des_Frankfurter_Paradiesg%C3%A4rtleins_001.jpg